          "sep": "+",
          "caption": "a monomial is ONE term"
        }
      },
      "choices": [
        "−7x²y",
        "3x + 2",
        "x² − 4",
        "5/x"
      ],
      "answer": "−7x²y",
      "acceptable": [],
      "hints": [
        "A monomial is <b>one term</b>: a number, a variable, or a number times variables (with whole-number exponents).",
        "A + or − between pieces splits it into more than one term.",
        "Dividing by a variable (5/x) is not allowed in a monomial."
      ],
      "solution": "3x + 2 and x² − 4 each have two terms (they are binomials). 5/x divides by x, so it is not a monomial.<br><b>−7x²y</b> is one term: −7 · x · x · y."
    },
